{title: The LORD Looks at the Heart}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 16:1–13}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Old Samuel came to Bethlehem with [Eb]a horn of oil in [Bb]hand
Jesse lined [Gm]up all his sons, [Eb]the finest in the land
[F][Bb]Eliab stood the [Eb]tallest, he [Gm]looked every inch a king
But [Eb]the LORD said, not this one, I'm [F]looking at a different thing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]The LORD does [F]not see as man [Gm]sees [Gm7/F]
[Eb]Man looks at [Bb]the outward appear[F]ance
But the [Eb]LORD looks at the heart
The [F]LORD looks at the [Bb]heart
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Seven sons went walking by, [Eb]and seven times God said [Bb]no
Are [Gm]these all the young [Eb]men you have, [Bb]the prophet asked him [F]slow
[Eb]There is still the youngest, he [Gm]is out tending the sheep
[Eb]Send for him, we will not sit down, [F]this promise God will keep
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Rise and anoint him, [Bb]this is the one
[F]The shepherd boy with the dust of the [Bb]hills
[Bb/D][Eb]And from that day on the Spirit of the [Gm]LORD
Came [Eb]powerfully upon [F]David
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Bb]LORD [F/A]looks at the [Gm7]heart
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
